```

## Structured Logging for CloudWatch

```java
// Use JSON logging — easier to filter in CloudWatch Logs Insights
// logback-spring.xml or via dependency: logstash-logback-encoder
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(GlobalExceptionHandler.class);

    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handle(Exception ex, HttpServletRequest req) {
        log.error("Unhandled error",
            kv("path", req.getRequestURI()),
            kv("method", req.getMethod()),
            kv("errorType", ex.getClass().getSimpleName()),
            ex);
        return ResponseEntity.status(500).body(new ErrorResponse(ex.getMessage()));
    }
}
```

```
# CloudWatch Logs Insights query — find top errors in last hour
fields @timestamp, errorType, path
| filter level = 'ERROR'
| stats count(*) as errorCount by errorType, path
| sort errorCount desc
| limit 20
```

